NATIONAL ASSEMBLY SECRETARIAT
ORDERS OF THE DAYfor the meeting of the National Assembly to be held on Thursday, the 23'd )anuary,2025 at 2.00 p.m1. Tilowot, Hodith, Noot and national anthem.QUESTIONS2. Questions entered in a separate list to be asked and answers given.CAttING ATTENTION NOTICE
3. MS. ASIYA NAZ TANOLI MR. AqEEL MALIKMR. IBRAR AHMAD to invite attention of the Minister for Defence to a matter ofurgent public importance regarding non-opening of more Federal Government Schools in DistrictRawalpindi, causing grave concern amongst the public.
MOTION
4. MS. SHAZA FATIMA KHAWAJA, Minister of State for lnformation Technology andTelecom munication to move under rule 288 ofthe Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in theNational Assembly, 2007 that the requirement of sub-rule (2) of rule 123 of the said Rules bedispensed with in order to take into consideration the Digital Nation Pakistan 8il1,2024.
LEGISLATIVE BUSINESS
5. MS. SHAZA FATIMA KHAWAJ& Minister of State for lnformation Technology andTelecom munication to move that the Bill to provide for the transformation of Pakistan into a digitalnation, enabling a digital society, digital economy, and digital governance [The Digital Nation PakistanBil,20241, as reported by the Standing Committee, be taken into consideration at once.6. MS. SHAZA FATIMA KHAWAJA, Minister of State for lnformation Technology andTelecommunication to move that the Bill to provide for the transformation of Pakistan into a digitalnation, enabling a digital society, digital economy, and digital governance [The Digital Nation PakistanBill, 20241, be passed.
PERIODICAL REPORT OF THE STANDING CO
M
M
ITTEE - PRESENTATION OF:
7. MR. PULLAIN, Chairman Standing Committee on lnformation and Broadcasting to present thePeriodical Report of the Committee for the period !'t July, 2024 to 31't December, 2024, as requiredby rule 234-4 ofthe Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in the NationalAssembly, 2007.
MATTERS OTHERTHAN POINTS OF ORDER
9. MR. MUHAMMAD ALI SARFRAZ to invite attention of the Minister for National HealthServices, Regulations and Coordination to a matter of urgent public importance regarding non-recognition of professional medical articles by PMDC already published in the medical journals,causing grave concern amongst the public.
TAHIR HUSSAINSecretary General
Raising matters under Rule 18 which are not Points of Order.CAttING ATTENTION NOTICE
8.
lslamabad, the22nd lanuary, 2025

